=== Natural generation ===
Acacia leaves occur naturally on [[acacia]] trees in [[savanna]]s. They also generate as part of [[abandoned camp]]s in savannas.

{{block distribution}}

=== Post-generation ===
{{see also|Tutorial:Tree farming}}
Acacia leaves generate as part of acacia trees grown from [[acacia sapling]]s.

== Usage ==
{{Main|Leaves#Usage}}
Acacia leaves that decay have the same drop chances as when broken by players, yielding [[acacia sapling]]s 5% ({{frac|1|20}}) of the time, [[stick]]s 2% of the time, and otherwise nothing. Leaves that are burned do not yield saplings.

=== Smelting ingredient ===
{{Smelting
|showname=1
|Acacia Leaves
|Leaf Litter
|0.1}}

=== Redstone component ===
{{Exclusive|java|section=1}}
The state of a leaves block—including a player-placed block—changes after 1 game tick (half a redstone tick) when the distance to the nearest [[log]] or [[wood]] block changes, up to 6 blocks of leaves away. [[Observer]]s facing away from the leaves detect this change and transmit a redstone signal in the same game tick, making leaves useful for redstone signal transmission.

=== Piston interactivity ===
Leaves are destroyed when pushed by [[piston]]s. They do not stick to [[sticky piston]]s, [[slime block]]s, or [[honey block]]s.

=== Composting ===
Acacia of leaves have a 30% chance of increasing the compost level in a [[composter]] by 1. A stack of leaves yields an average of 3.05 [[bone meal]].

